.TH REMDBG 1 "September 2026" "REM developer tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
remdbg \- debug a single REM Linux process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remdbg
.I program
[\fIargument ...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B remdbg
launches a REM ELF under ptrace and provides breakpoints, register and memory
inspection, stepping, symbol lookup and a heuristic backtrace. It is a
guest-native process debugger, not a QEMU machine debugger and not a GDB
remote-protocol server.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Start or restart the current debuggee.
.TP
.B continue
Resume until exit, signal or a breakpoint.
.TP
.B break SYMBOL|ADDRESS
Set a software breakpoint.
.TP
.B regs
Show general registers and the nearest ELF symbol.
.TP
.B mem ADDRESS LENGTH
Read bytes from the tracee.
.TP
.B write ADDRESS BYTE
Write one byte to the tracee.
.TP
.B disasm [ADDRESS [COUNT]]
Disassemble fixed-width REM32 instructions.
.TP
.B step
Execute one instruction through ptrace single-step.
.TP
.B bt
Show PC, LR, and heuristic code-pointer candidates from a bounded stack area.
.TP
.B source, locals, globals
Show the supported subset of DWARF/source information. These commands may
invoke guest \fBreadelf\fR.
.TP
.B load FILE
Replace the stopped debuggee and load another program.
.TP
.B quit
Exit the debugger.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
remdbg ./hello
(remdbg) break main
(remdbg) run
(remdbg) regs
(remdbg) step
(remdbg) continue
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
Only one process/thread is traced. The backtrace beyond PC/LR is heuristic.
DWARF evaluation is limited; current GCC output has a documented stack-local
location mismatch, and the tested chibicc artifact did not emit a source CU.
The exact kernel, debugger and rootfs must be a qualified matching tuple.
.SH SEE ALSO
readelf(1), objdump(1), remdbg documentation in REM_DEBUGGER.md
